gnal analysis. Within Signal Representation, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of complex exponentials within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Signal Representation module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of complex exponentials, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'complex exponentials; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of complex exponentials, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000904', 'linearity', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'A system property in which scaling and addition of inputs produce correspondingly scaled and added outputs.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of linearity within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of linearity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'A system property in which scaling and addition of inputs produce correspondingly scaled and added outputs. Within Linear Time-Invariant Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of linearity within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of linearity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'linearity; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of linearity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000905', 'time invariance', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'A system property in which shifting the input in time produces the same shift in the output.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of time invariance within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of time invariance, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'A system property in which shifting the input in time produces the same shift in the output. Within Linear Time-Invariant Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of time invariance within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of time invariance, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'time invariance; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of time invariance, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000906', 'convolution', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'An operation that combines an input signal with a system impulse response to obtain the output of an LTI system.