lse input and a complete characterisation of an LTI system. Within Linear Time-Invariant Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of impulse response within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of impulse response, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'impulse response; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of impulse response, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000908', 'system properties', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'Characteristics such as linearity, time invariance, causality, stability, and memory used to classify systems.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of system properties within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of system properties, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Characteristics such as linearity, time invariance, causality, stability, and memory used to classify systems. Within Linear Time-Invariant Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of system properties within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Linear Time-Invariant Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of system properties, 