 for which a Z-transform or related transform converges. Within Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of ROC within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of ROC, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'ROC; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of ROC, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000916', 'difference equations', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'Discrete-time equations relating current and past input or output samples.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of difference equations within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of difference equations, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Discrete-time equations relating current and past input or output samples. Within Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of difference equations within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of difference equations, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'difference equations; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of difference equations, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000917', 'digital-system response', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'Output behaviour of a discrete-time system for specified inputs and initial conditions.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of digital-system response within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of digital-system response, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Output behaviour of a discrete-time system for specified inputs and initial conditions. Within Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of digital-system response within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of digital-system response, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'digital-system response; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of digital-system response, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000918', 'Nyquist rate', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', '