ction, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'reconstruction; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of reconstruction, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000921', 'quantization', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'Mapping continuous-amplitude or high-resolution sample values to a finite set of discrete levels.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of quantization within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Sampling and Reconstruction module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of quantization, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Mapping continuous-amplitude or high-resolution sample values to a finite set of discrete levels. Within Sampling and Reconstruction, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of quantization within Signals and Systems, particularly where the Sampling and Reconstruction module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of quantization, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'quantization; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of quantization, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Signals and Systems', 'Active'), ('KCR_000922', 'frequency response', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Signals and Systems', 'Technical Concept', 'System gain an